    "25-year-old postpartum woman developed low-grade fever and abdominal pain in the third week after cesarean delivery with tubal sterilization.",
    "She was hospitalized after persistent fever for 1 week with progressive abdominal pain.",
    "Vital signs on admission were temperature 39.0 C, heart rate 112/min, respiratory rate 26/min, and blood pressure 110/60 mmHg.",
    "Abdominal examination showed left lower quadrant tenderness with guarding and rebound tenderness.",
    "Pelvic examination revealed a large amount of purulent vaginal discharge, marked cervical excitation pain, a bulging cul-de-sac, and a tender pelvic mass.",
    "Labs showed WBC 33,170/mm3 with 90.2% polymorphonuclear cells, hematocrit 32.2%, platelets 422,000/mm3, BUN 6.2 mg/dL, creatinine 0.5 mg/dL, potassium 3.4 mmol/L, and bicarbonate 22 mmol/L.",
    "Ultrasound demonstrated a left adnexal multiloculated mass measuring 6.2 x 8.2 x 10.9 cm and approximately 50 mL of free fluid."
  ],
